The change (one implementation file)
  harness/model-guide/review-run.sh:

    -if [ ! -d "$SET_DIR/src" ]; then
    -  refuse "the set has no src folder"
    -fi
    -shopt -s nullglob
    -DIFF_PATHS=("$SET_DIR/src"/*.diff)
    +if [ ! -d "$SET_DIR/diffs" ]; then
    +  refuse "the set has no diffs folder"
    +fi
    +shopt -s nullglob
    +DIFF_PATHS=("$SET_DIR/diffs"/*.diff)

  A new 3-line comment states that `diffs/` is the review input (spec D7),
  and that `src/` holds the source copies without the plants.
  The pass loop and the probe loop both read `DIFF_PATHS`, so one glob
  serves both modes. The folder check and the glob sit before the lock, the
  pass number, and every call, so a set with no seeded diff writes no pass
  record and makes no call.
  `grep -n "src" harness/model-guide/review-run.sh` prints the new comment
  only. No comment names `src/` as the review input.

